# text = My mother , being at once highly accomplished , well informed , and fond of employment , took the whole charge of our education on herself , with the exception of Latin -- which my father undertook to teach us -- so that we never even went to school ; and , as there was no society in the neighbourhood , our only intercourse with the world consisted in a stately tea-party , now and then , with the principal farmers and tradespeople of the vicinity ( just to avoid being stigmatized as too proud to consort with our neighbours ), and an annual visit to our paternal grandfather's ; where himself , our kind grandmamma , a maiden aunt , and two or three elderly ladies and gentlemen , were the only persons we ever saw .
# sent_id = 17
