# text = Happily , however , during that spring , they never , but once , got anything but empty nests , or eggs -- being too impatient to leave them till the birds were hatched ; that once , Tom , who had been with his uncle into the neighbouring plantation , came running in high glee into the garden , with a brood of little callow nestlings in his hands .
