# text = It was with a strange feeling of desolation , mingled with a strong sense of the novelty of my situation , and a joyless kind of curiosity concerning what was yet unknown , that I awoke the next morning ; feeling like one whirled away by enchantment , and suddenly dropped from the clouds into a remote and unknown land , widely and completely isolated from all he had ever seen or known before ; or like a thistle-seed borne on the wind to some strange nook of uncongenial soil , where it must lie long enough before it can take root and germinate , extracting nourishment from what appears so alien to its nature : if , indeed , it ever can .
