# text = There was no member of it in whom I regretted this sad want of principle so much as Miss Murray herself ; not only because she had taken a fancy to me , but because there was so much of what was pleasant and prepossessing in herself , that , in spite of her failings , I really liked her -- when she did not rouse my indignation , or ruffle my temper by TOO great a display of her faults .
