# text = Of fancy-work I knew nothing but what I gathered from my pupil and my own observation ; but no sooner was I initiated , than she made me useful in twenty different ways : all the tedious parts of her work were shifted on to my shoulders ; such as stretching the frames , stitching in the canvas , sorting the wools and silks , putting in the grounds , counting the stitches , rectifying mistakes , and finishing the pieces she was tired of .
