# text = As an animal , Matilda was all right , full of life , vigour , and activity ; as an intelligent being , she was barbarously ignorant , indocile , careless and irrational ; and , consequently , very distressing to one who had the task of cultivating her understanding , reforming her manners , and aiding her to acquire those ornamental attainments which , unlike her sister , she despised as much as the rest .
