# text = I sometimes felt myself degraded by the life I led , and ashamed of submitting to so many indignities ; and sometimes I thought myself a fool for caring so much about them , and feared I must be sadly wanting in Christian humility , or that charity which But , with time and patience , matters began to be slightly ameliorated : slowly , it is true , and almost imperceptibly ; but I got rid of my male pupils ( that was no trifling advantage ), and the girls , as I intimated before concerning one of them , became a little less insolent , and began to show some symptoms of esteem
