# text = Often , when they had no more agreeable occupation at hand , the Misses Murray would amuse themselves with visiting the poor cottagers on their father's estate , to receive their flattering homage , or to hear the old stories or gossiping news of the garrulous old women ; or , perhaps , to enjoy the purer pleasure of making the poor people happy with their cheering presence and their occasional gifts , so easily bestowed , so thankfully received .
