# text = She was seated beside her little fire ( consisting of a few red cinders and a bit of stick ), busily knitting , with a small sackcloth cushion at her feet , placed for the accommodation of her gentle friend the cat , who was seated thereon , with her long tail half encircling her velvet paws , and her half-closed eyes dreamily gazing on the low , crooked fender replied she , rising to welcome me with a contented smile ; which I was glad to see , for Nancy had been somewhat afflicted with religious melancholy .
