# text = I hastened back to Horton Lodge , where , having entered the schoolroom , I found the tea-table all in confusion , the tray flooded with slops , and Miss Matilda in a most ferocious humour replied I ( and , indeed , the thought of its driving her home had never entered my head I bore her coarse reproaches with astonishing equanimity , even with cheerfulness ; for I was sensible that I had done more good to Nancy Brown than harm to her : and perhaps some other thoughts assisted to keep up my spirits , and impart a relish to the cup of cold , overdrawn tea , and a charm to the otherwise unsightly table ; and -- I had almost said -- to Miss Matilda's unamiable face .
