# text = Every blow that shakes it will serve to harden it against a future stroke ; as constant labour thickens the skin of the hand , and strengthens its muscles instead of wasting them away : so that a day of arduous toil , that might excoriate a lady's palm , would make no sensible impression on that of a hardy ploughman said I replied he We now approached a stile communicating with a footpath that conducted to a farm-house , where , I suppose , Mr . Weston purposed to make himself for he presently took leave of me , crossed the stile , and traversed the path with his usual firm , elastic tread , leaving me to ponder his words as I continued my course alone .
