# text = Soon after breakfast Miss Matilda , having galloped and blundered through a few unprofitable lessons , and vengeably thumped the piano for an hour , in a terrible humour with both me and it , because her mamma would not give her a holiday , had betaken herself to her favourite places of resort , the yards , the stables , and the dog-kennels ; and Miss Murray was gone forth to enjoy a quiet ramble with a new fashionable novel for her companion , leaving me in the schoolroom hard at work upon a water-colour drawing which I had promised to do for her , and which she insisted upon my finishing that day .
