# text = The fact was she had purchased it when but a small puppy , insisting at first that no one should touch it but herself ; but soon becoming tired of so helpless and troublesome a nursling , she had gladly yielded to my entreaties to be allowed to take charge of it ; and I , by carefully nursing the little creature from infancy to adolescence , of course , had obtained its affections : a reward I should have greatly valued , and looked upon as far outweighing all the trouble I had had with it , had not poor Snap's grateful feelings exposed him to many a harsh word and many a spiteful kick and pinch from his owner , and were he not now in danger of being ' put away ' in consequence , or transferred to some rough , stony - hearted master .
