# text = He greeted me in his usual quiet , unaffected way , stopped to inquire about the condition of the sick man and his family , and with a sort of unconscious , brotherly disregard to ceremony took from my hand the book out of which I had been reading , turned over its pages , made a few brief but very sensible remarks , and restored it ; then told me about some poor sufferer he had just been visiting , talked a little about Nancy Brown , made a few observations upon my little rough friend the terrier , that was frisking at his feet , and finally upon the beauty of the weather , and departed .
