# text = None of the Murrays were disposed to attend church in the afternoon , excepting Rosalie : she was bent upon going as usual ; so she ordered the carriage , and I went with her : nothing loth , of course , for at church I might look without fear of scorn or censure upon a form and face more pleasing to me than the most beautiful of God's creations ; I might listen without disturbance to a voice more charming than the sweetest music to my ears ; I might seem to hold communion with that soul in which I felt so deeply interested , and imbibe its purest thoughts and holiest aspirations , with no alloy to such felicity except the secret reproaches of my conscience , which would too often whisper that I was deceiving my own self , and mocking God with the service of a heart more bent upon the creature than the Creator .
