# text = As well might the humble glowworm despise that power of giving light without which the roving fly might pass her and repass her a thousand times , and never rest beside her : she might hear her winged darling buzzing over and around her ; he vainly seeking her , she longing to be found , but with no power to make her presence known , no voice to call him , no wings to follow his flight ;-- the fly must seek another mate , the worm must live and die alone .
