# text = Had I seen it depicted in a novel , I should have thought it unnatural ; had I heard it described by others , I should have deemed it a mistake or an exaggeration ; but when I saw it with my own eyes , and suffered from it too , I could only conclude that excessive vanity , like drunkenness , hardens the heart , enslaves the faculties , and perverts the feelings ; and that dogs are not the only creatures which , when gorged to the throat , will yet gloat over what they cannot devour , and grudge the smallest morsel to a starving brother .
