# text = Now , also , she was denied the solace which the companionship of the coachman , grooms , horses , greyhounds , and pointers might have afforded ; for her mother having , notwithstanding the disadvantages of a country life , so satisfactorily disposed of her elder daughter , the pride of her heart had begun seriously to turn her attention to the younger ; and , being truly alarmed at the roughness of her manners , and thinking it high time to work a reform , had been roused at length to exert her authority , and prohibited entirely the yards , stables , kennels , and coach-house .
